Q: Explain in one short paragraph what KV cache compression means in transformer inference.
A:  KV cache compression in transformer inference refers to techniques that reduce the memory footprint of key-value (KV) cache used during inference, without compromising the accuracy of the model's output. This is achieved by compressing the cached values while maintaining their integrity, allowing for more efficient use of memory and enabling the processing of longer sequences or larger batch sizes without running out of memory. This is particularly important for deploying large language models on devices with limited memory resources.

